.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-TEMPLATE\-LIST" "1" "" "roark-simulation-template-list" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-template\-list \- List simulation templates
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation template list
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Returns the built\-in simulation templates, each resolved against this project: the metric and check definitions it collects, and the flows it runs with the variants it covers. A template is a preset rather than a stored object, so building a run from one produces an ordinary run plan you own and can edit afterwards. Pass a `slug` as `template` to POST /v1/simulation/run. Every entry is complete, so there is no per\-template endpoint to follow up with, and the list is a fixed catalogue rather than a paginated one. Only templates a request can actually run are listed.
.SH "API"
GET /v1/simulation/template
